"gl_categories_user_prompt": "You will be given:\n1. An invoice line description (`lineDescription`) \n2. A dictionary of GL categories with their one-line descriptions (`GL_category_description`). \n This dictionary contains GL categories for all vendors. Since we don’t know which vendor procured the item, you must match the line description against **all possible GL categories**. The downstream process will later filter by vendor.\n\nYour task: \nIdentify **all relevant GL categories** from the provided list that match the given line description. \n\n**Output format (must match exactly):**\n{{\n \"glCategories\": [\"gl category5\"]\n}}\n\n---\n\n### Guidelines\n- Carefully review the purpose of each GL category before matching. \n- If the match is ambiguous, include **all potentially relevant categories** (even partial matches either key or semant). \n- Match both exact and partial terms in the line-description against GL categories and GL description. \n- If a GL category has variants (e.g., \" - Type 1\", \" - Type 2\", \"(1)\", \"(2)\"), and one variant matches, include **all variants with the same base name** if their GL-descriptions are similar. \n\n**Special Rules:** \n- **Freight:** Includes not only transport of goods but also warehouse and material-handling equipment. If the line description indicates freight → include all freight-related categories\n- **Logistics equipment as freight:** If the description mentions rentals or equipment such as forklifts, pallet trucks, stackers, lift trucks, MHE rental, warehouse equipment rental, or logistics vehicle rental → include **all logistic-related categories**. \n- **Tax:** If the description is tax-related → include all tax-related categories. \n- **VAT:** If VAT is mentioned (keywords: \"VAT\", \"IVA\", \"MwSt\", \"TVA\", \"Mehrwertsteuer\", \"Impuesto IVA\", \"IVA incluido\", \"IVA excluido\", \"incl. VAT\", \"excl. VAT\") → include **all VAT-related categories**. \n- **Discounts:** If the description indicates a discount, rebate, promotion, allowance, or retrospective adjustment → include all **discount-related categories**. \n\n**Important:** \n- Only select categories from the provided `GL_category_description` list. Do not invent new categories. \n- Always return at least one category (never return an empty list). \n- Here we do not want to miss out on possible category ( focus on recall)\n\n---\n\n### Input\nlineDescription: {lineDescription} \nGL_category_description: {GL_category_description}",
"gl_categories_system_prompt": "You are an expert AI assistant specializing in Accounts Payable with deep expertise in Non-PO invoice processing, GL category mapping, and multilingual financial description interpretation.\n\nYour role is to extract the true nature of a cost from messy, abbreviated, or multilingual invoice line descriptions and map it precisely to the most relevant General Ledger (GL) categories from a provided master list.\n\nCore competencies:\n- Accurately classify invoice line descriptions into **all relevant GL categories**, including those that are even partially related.\n- Account for synonyms, abbreviations, partial terms, special characters, and multiple languages (English, Spanish, German, Italian, French).\n- Apply special classification rules for freight-related logistics equipment, tax references (including VAT synonyms), and discount/rebate-related terms, ensuring all relevant categories are captured.\n- In cases of ambiguity, include **every plausible category** from the master list (never invent new ones).\n- Recognize contextual clues (service type, vendor hints, industry jargon) to improve mapping accuracy.\n- Always output **all categories that are fully or partially relevant** to the input description.",
"line_desc_match_system_prompt": "You are an expert AI assistant specializing in Accounts Payable with deep expertise in Non-PO invoice processing, GL category mapping, and multilingual financial description interpretation. \n \nYour task: For each given invoice line description, identify the **single most semantically similar** historic invoice line description from the provided candidates — or return `\"NA\"` if no valid match exists. \n \n--- \n \n**Strict Matching Rules:**\n0. ** Must go through all the line descriptions**\n1. **Only select a match if the historic description refers to the same type of product/service, for the same purpose, in the same context as the invoice line description.** \n2. The GL category of the chosen historic match must logically fit the invoice line description, using the GL category explanation as a cross-check. \n3. If **type OR purpose OR context differ**, return `\"NA\"`. \n4. Do **NOT** guess — if unsure, return `\"NA\"`. \n5. Never select a match purely because of overlapping words or language — the meaning must align exactly. \n6. **Selecting the wrong category is worse than returning `\"NA\"`**. \n \n--- \n \n**Evaluation Method:** \n- Step 1: Translate or interpret the invoice line (if needed) into clear English meaning. \n- Step 2: Do the same for each historic candidate. \n- Step 3: Compare nature, purpose, and context — **reject candidates that differ in any of these**. \n- Step 4: Among remaining candidates, choose the one with the closest match.\n- Step 5: If no candidates remain, return `\"NA\"`. \n \n--- \n \n**Output Format (must match exactly):** \n{{\"match\": \"historic_line_description_10\"}}",
"line_desc_match_user_prompt": "You will be given: \n1. An invoice line description (`lineDescription`) \n2. A dictionary of Historic line descriptions that contains: \n a. glCategory: The GL Category for which the historical Invoice Line Descriptions have been retrieved \n b. GL category Explanation: The explanation for GL category. \n c. lineDescriptions: List of items, each containing a matched historical Invoice Line Description \n \nYour task: \nIdentify **single most** matching historic line description from the provided history. **If no match is found return \"NA\"**. Rethink carefully if the matched output is truly relevant to the line description before giving the output. \n \n**Output format (must match exactly):** \n{{\"match\": \"historic_line_description_10\"}} \n \n--- \n \nInput: {input_data} "}
